"not significant","donor_padj":0.819497,"donor_log2fc":-0.182054,"donor_lfcse":0.211495,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00193105},{"cell_type":"Mic","gene_symbol":"FA2H","gene_symbol_current":"FA2H","gene_id":"ENSG00000103089","nucleus_tested":false,"nucleus_significant":null,"nucleus_direction":"not tested","nucleus_padj":null,"nucleus_log2fc":null,"nucleus_score":null,"pct_ad":null,"pct_control":null,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.454451,"donor_log2fc":-0.583457,"donor_lfcse":0.292857,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.0149331},{"cell_type":"OPC","gene_symbol":"FA2H","gene_symbol_current":"FA2H","gene_id":"ENSG00000103089","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.0404212,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.102811,"nucleus_score":-2.50852,"pct_ad":0.477035,"pct_control":0.494496,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.0632185,"donor_lfcse":0.103956,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":2.2931e-06},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"FA2H","gene_symbol_current":"FA2H","gene_id":"ENSG00000103089","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":true,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":1.74313e-36,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.140383,"nucleus_score":-12.7767,"pct_ad":0.812126,"pct_control":0.838625,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.868586,"donor_log2fc":-0.0868431,"donor_lfcse":0.0964466,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.00954966}],"modules":[{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_id":"ENSG00000103089","module":"blue","kme":0.251951,"hub":false,"module_direction":"higher in AD","module_padj":0.842971,"module_significant":false}],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000103089","entrez_id":["79152"],"uniprot":["Q7L5A8"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a protein that catalyzes the synthesis of 2-hydroxysphingolipids, a subset of sphingolipids that contain 2-hydroxy fatty acids. Sphingolipids play roles in many cellular processes and their structural diversity arises from modification of the hydrophobic ceramide moiety, such as by 2-hydroxylation of the N-acyl chain, and the existence of many different head groups. Mutations in this gene have been associated with leukodystrophy dysmyelinating with spastic paraparesis with or without dystonia.[provided by RefSeq, Mar 2010].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q7L5A8","text":"Catalyzes the hydroxylation of free fatty acids at the C-2 position to produce 2-hydroxy fatty acids, which are building blocks of sphingolipids and glycosphingolipids common in neural tissue and epidermis (PubMed:15337768, PubMed:15863841, PubMed:17355976, PubMed:22517924). FA2H is stereospecific for the production of (R)-2-hydroxy fatty acids (PubMed:22517924). Plays an essential role in the synthesis of galactosphingolipids of the myelin sheath (By similarity). Responsible for the synthesis of sphingolipids and glycosphingolipids involved in the formation of epidermal lamellar bodies critical for skin permeability barrier (PubMed:17355976). Participates in the synthesis of glycosphingolipids and a fraction of type II wax diesters in sebaceous gland, specifically regulating hair follicle homeostasis (By similarity). Involved in the synthesis of sphingolipids of plasma membrane rafts, controlling lipid raft mobility and trafficking of raft-associated proteins (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}